   ClearRect = 25,
+  // Publish a UBO slice as "previous slice, plus the bytes that changed".
+  // Mario Kart Wii rewrites 4112-byte VertexShaderConstants 361 times a frame
+  // while only ~172 bytes of each differ, so the full-block upload moves 2.39 GB
+  // across a run to convey 0.100 GB of change.
+  //
+  // The unchanged bytes exist only in the previous slice on the GPU, so they are
+  // carried forward with a device-side copy. That copy CANNOT simply be an
+  // encoder command next to an ordinary UploadBuffer: uploads go out through
+  // queue.writeBuffer, which lands on the queue timeline before the render
+  // encoder is submitted, so a copy inside the encoder would run after every
+  // write of the frame and clobber them. The consumer therefore does all three
+  // steps itself, in order: writeBuffer the delta into a staging buffer, then
+  // copy previous->new and staging->new inside the encoder.
+  //   u0=ringId u1=newOff u2=prevOff u3=blockSize u4=deltaOff u5=deltaLen
+  //   u6=srcHeapPtr
